<title>INDIA: India RBI sets interest for FRB 1999 at 14.13 pct.</title>
<headline>India RBI sets interest for FRB 1999 at 14.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The interest rate on the floating rate bonds (FRB) 1999 has been set at 14.13 percent for the half year ending March 29, 1997, the Reserve Bank of India said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bonds were issued in 1995 with a clause offering interest at a mark-up of 1.25 percent over the average rate of the implicit cut-off yields for 364 day treasury bills auctioned during the preceding half-year.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 900</p>
</text>
